# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Velthy Party — environment
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you need. Everything here has a
# working default in code; the file only exists to override. NOTHING in this
# file is required for the server to start.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. Do not commit it — the tunnel token is a credential.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Server ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Port the process listens on. Pterodactyl sets SERVER_PORT; PORT wins if both
# are present. Falls back to 8080.
#
# This deployment's host provides only 33183 / 37720 / 25620, so 33183 is the
# one in use. Whatever is set here must match the tunnel's Public Hostname
# service in the Cloudflare dashboard — see the tunnel section at the bottom.
PORT=33183

# NODE_ENV=production

# --- Party behaviour (all optional; the defaults are the documented ones) ---

# Devices allowed in one party.
# JAM_MAX_MEMBERS=5

# How often the server re-states playback state to everyone, unprompted.
# JAM_STATE_HEARTBEAT_MS=5000

# How far ahead a resume is scheduled, so every device aims at one instant.
# JAM_PLAY_LEAD_MS=350

# How long a dropped socket keeps its slot.
# JAM_DISCONNECT_GRACE_MS=45000

# Empty-party reaping, and the hard ceiling on any party's life.
# JAM_EMPTY_PARTY_TTL_MS=120000
# JAM_PARTY_MAX_AGE_MS=43200000

# Per-member control token bucket, and the queue size ceiling.
# JAM_CONTROL_RATE_PER_SECOND=25
# JAM_MAX_QUEUE_LENGTH=500

# Browser origins allowed to open a socket. Empty allows any, which is what the
# Android app needs (it sends no Origin header).
# JAM_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# --- Updating this server from the repository -----------------------------
#
# Nothing needs to be set here. The server follows its own repository by
# default, and the three values it needs are compiled in:
#
#   repository  https://github.com/Synxx12/velthy.git
#   branch      main
#   subfolder   backend-nest      (this project is one folder of a monorepo)
#
# So a deployment updates itself on every restart with no configuration at all:
# it fetches, copies this folder out of the repository, reinstalls if the
# lockfile moved, and rebuilds. The log says which of those happened:
#
#   [startup] updated to 07747ac: 3 file(s) changed.
#   [startup] already current at 07747ac -- nothing changed.
#
# `node_modules/`, `.env`, and anything put here by hand survive every update.
#
# ## The three overrides, for a fork or a different branch
#
#   GIT_URL=https://github.com/you/your-fork.git
#   GIT_BRANCH=develop
#   GIT_SUBDIR=server
#
# ## Turning it off
#
#   GIT_PULL=0
#
# A development tree does this by itself: a folder that sits inside somebody
# else's checkout is never updated, because the sources there are uncommitted
# edits. `GIT_PULL=1` forces it on anywhere.
#
# ## Checking what is actually running
#
# Whatever way the code arrives, this answers "is the deploy current?" from
# outside the machine:
#
#   npm run version
#   npm run version -- https://api.velthy.my.id
#
# or by hand — the banner names the build and every capability it has:
#
#   curl -s https://api.velthy.my.id/ | jq

# --- Cloudflare Tunnel ----------------------------------------------------
#
# The tunnel token from Cloudflare Zero Trust:
#   Networks -> Tunnels -> Create a tunnel -> Cloudflared -> copy the token.
#
# It is used by `npm run tunnel` (scripts/tunnel.mjs). The token is a
# credential — it lets anyone run the tunnel — so this is the one value in this
# file that must never leave the machine.
#
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=eyJhIjoi...
#
# There is deliberately no TUNNEL_ORIGIN here. A token tunnel is managed
# remotely: the origin it forwards to and the public hostname it answers on are
# both set in the Cloudflare dashboard (Networks -> Tunnels -> this tunnel ->
# Public Hostname), NOT in this file. Nothing in scripts/tunnel.mjs reads an
# origin from the environment.
#
# The dashboard entry for this deployment is:
#   Public hostname : api.velthy.my.id
#   Service         : HTTP -> localhost:33183   (the PORT above)
